<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Oxford Book of Carols</span><span class="sg-chain-h">printed from William Grattan Flood's transcription</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wexford Carol (Julie Andrews)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording with an additional verse</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wexford Carol (Loreena McKennitt)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1987</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Chieftains Celebration (The Chieftains, with Nanci Griffith)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Wexford Carol (John Rutter, the Cambridge Singers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Songs of Joy &amp; Peace (Yo-Yo Ma, with Alison Krauss)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Wexford Carols (Caitríona O'Leary)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2014</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title track of a collection of traditional Irish carols</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hallelujah! (Mormon Tabernacle Choir)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2016</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement by Mack Wilberg</span></li></ul></section>
